  data: {
    LLM: "If your hand has fewer than two trumps and no 'safe' doubles (like 6-6), folding is the optimal move.\n\nUse the dummy hand only if you are already at a high score (e.g., 12+) since the risk of being rounced is mitigated by the potential for a fresh 5-tile set.\n\nDefensive play: If you are close to 0, play conservatively to avoid being rounced, which could set you back multiple rounds.",
